# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 7 — the CALIBRATION PAIR for CI-PARITY-GATE-ROT.29 acceptance (d),
# as a tracked artifact rather than as a claim about a commit that does not exist.
#
# WHAT THIS PATCH REINTRODUCES. `GuardChain::summary` originally built its `positions` string from the
# PLAN's two booleans (`self.loop_guard` / `self.trailing_guard`) and ran BEFORE `apply_plan`. That is
# an honest answer to "what did the planner INTEND" and says nothing about what was EMITTED — so the
# bank rows that pin the emission (D9/D10) could not see a defect in it.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT IN GIT HISTORY, AND WHY THAT MATTERED. The defect was found and fixed inside one
# slice, so it was never committed — which made `.29`'s first draft of acceptance (d) cite a
# "RED/GREEN pair in git" that a future implementer could not find. Shipping the patch makes the pair
# real. ⛔ The general lesson is the leaf's own: a defect fixed before commit leaves NO reproducer
# behind unless one is deliberately preserved, and a gate calibrated against a defect needs the
# defect.
#
# THE 2x2, MEASURED (2026-08-14, session #230). The second column is the plant that DELETES the
# trailing-lookahead emission in `apply_plan` (`if false && chain.trailing_guard`):
#
#   summary source        | + emission plant | guard_dry_run/probe.sh
#   ----------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------------
#   plan-derived (THIS)   | yes              | 16/16 GREEN  <- WRONG: reports [loop+trailing]
#                         |                  |    for a rule whose body has no trailing lookahead
#   tree-derived (HEAD)   | yes              | MISMATCH     <- RIGHT: D10 flips by name
#
# ⇒ a gate for acceptance (d) must be RED with this patch applied and GREEN without it.
#
# HOW TO RUN IT (from the repository root; the tree must be clean first):
#   git apply docs/tasks/artifacts/engine_universal_services/guard_dry_run/plan_derived_summary.patch
#   (cd rust && cargo build --features "generated_parsers ebnf_dual_run" --bin ast_pipeline)
#   bash docs/tasks/artifacts/engine_universal_services/guard_dry_run/probe.sh     # still 16/16
#   git checkout -- rust/src/ast_pipeline/indirect_lr_elimination.rs               # ⛔ tree must be clean
#
# ⛔ `git checkout --` DISCARDS uncommitted edits to that file — `.17` slice 6b lost work that way.
# Snapshot the file's CONTENT before applying if your tree is dirty, and compare hashes after.
#
# git apply ignores every line above the first `diff --git`, so this header is safe.
